Appendix A: Experimental Survey and Evaluation Instrument
A.1 Task Instructions for Annotators
Topic Interpretation and Keyword Salience Task
Overview:
You are presented with candidate word lists representing latent semantic topics extracted by a machine learning model. Your objective is to identify which keywords best capture the core semantic theme of the topic.
Instructions:
List Inspection: Carefully inspect the presented list of 20 candidate keywords.
Selection: Check the box next to each keyword that you consider an essential and coherent descriptor of the underlying topic. You may select as many or as few words as you deem appropriate (typically 2–5 words).
Thematic Labeling: Provide a brief (1–3 word) label that summarizes the main theme of the topic in the text field provided.
Confidence Rating: Rate your subjective confidence in your selection accuracy on the provided 5-point scale.
Submission: Click “Next Topic” to proceed. Please note that once a topic is submitted, your selections are final and cannot be modified.
________________________________________
A.2 Post-Task Evaluation Questionnaire
Please respond to the following statements based on your experience during the evaluation session.
Rating Scale:
1: Strongly Disagree | 2: Disagree | 3: Somewhat Disagree | 4: Neutral | 5: Somewhat Agree | 6: Agree | 7: Strongly Agree
Part 1: Cognitive Strategy & Visual Scanning Heuristics
Top-Down Primacy: “When evaluating a topic list, I primarily based my understanding on the first few words at the top of the list.”
Exhaustive Inspection: “I thoroughly evaluated all 20 candidate words from top to bottom before deciding which ones to select.”
Early Anchor Commitment: “Once I found 2 or 3 words that seemed to fit together near the beginning, I paid much less attention to the words placed further down.”
Weight/Importance Perception: “I assumed that the words placed at the top of the list were mathematically more important or more representative of the topic.”
Cognitive Fatigue: “Scanning through 20 keywords per topic became cognitively demanding as the session progressed.”
Part 2: Qualitative Feedback
Please provide brief answers to the following:
Strategy Description: “Briefly describe the strategy you used to decide which keywords to select when a list appeared ambiguous or mixed in theme.”
________________________________________
Pattern Observation: “Did you notice any instances where the most descriptive or relevant words were placed near the middle or end of the list? If yes, how did that affect your selection behavior?”
